    text: 'CLUBS & COMMITTEES\nEVENT CALENDAR\nNovember 2026 – March 2027\nProposed schedule | IIM Sirmaur\nThis is an intentionally staggered calendar rather than a fixed monthly rotation. Each club or committee has between one and three events across the period, with uneven spacing to keep the campus calendar varied and manageable.\nEvent schedule\nEvent allocation at a glance\nNote: Dates are tentative and can be adjusted around examinations, institute events, holidays, venue availability and club/committee readiness. The calendar is a planning proposal, not a confirmed schedule.\nDATE\nCLUB / COMMITTEE\nEVENT\nOVERVIEW\n14 November 2026\nKalakriti – Cultural Committee\nRangrez: Open Mic & Creative Showcase\nAn informal evening featuring music, poetry, stand-up, dance and other student performances.\n28 November 2026\nEconyx – Economics Club\nThe Bull Run: Market Simulation\nA fast-paced simulation where teams react to changing market conditions, news and economic indicators.\n9 December 2026\nMarkaizen – Marketing Club\nBrandstorm: The Rebranding Challenge\nTeams pick a familiar brand and pitch a refreshed identity, positioning and campaign idea.\n19 December 2026\nSports Committee\nWinter Inter-Hostel Football Cup\nA short-format football tournament bringing hostel teams together in a competitive campus event.\n10 January 2027\nSankalp – CSR Committee\nProject Warmth: Winter Donation Drive\nA collection and distribution initiative for winter clothing and essential supplies, supported by student volunteers.\n24 January 2027\nThe Dialectical Society – Debating Club\nClash of Claims: Parliamentary Debate\nA structured debate event with surprise motions, timed speeches and rebuttal rounds.\n30 January 2027\nSapient – Consulting & Strategy Club\nCase in Point: Live Consulting Challenge\nTeams analyse a business problem, develop recommendations and present their solution to a panel.\n7 February 2027\nMarkaizen – Marketing Club\nAd Mad: The 60-Second Campaign\nTeams create and present a short advertisement for an unexpected product or service.\n20 February 2027\nSports Committee\nSmash It: Inter-Batch Badminton Tournament\nSingles and doubles fixtures across batches, with a knockout format and finals.\n27 February 2027\nKalakriti – Cultural Committee\nAlaap: Acoustic & Unplugged Night\nA relaxed live-music evening centred on acoustic performances, collaborations and student-led acts.\n6 March 2027\nEconyx – Economics Club\nPolicyLab: The Budget Room\nA policy discussion and team challenge in which participants assess a budget scenario and defend their priorities.\n14 March 2027\nSankalp – CSR Committee\nGreen Campus: Sustainability Action Day\nA campus-focused initiative involving waste segregation awareness, clean-up activities and practical sustainability actions.\n26 March 2027\nSapient – Consulting & Strategy Club\nThe Boardroom: Strategy Showdown\nA final strategy competition where teams respond to a business disruption and defend their decisions before a judging panel.\nCLUB / COMMITTEE\nNO. OF EVENTS\nEconyx\n2\nMarkaizen\n2\nThe Dialectical Society\n1\nKalakriti\n2\nSports Committee\n2\nSankalp\n2\nSapient\n2\n',
