    summary:
      'Office contacts and 29 clubs/committees; BMS applicability and email routing flagged.',
    text: '# CampusOS – IIM Sirmaur BMS Data Research\n\nResearch notes compiled 2 November 2026 from the IIM Sirmaur website, Instagram search results and other public web pages. Items are marked as official, unverified or missing so they can be loaded into CampusOS with the right labels.\n\n## Summary\n\n- The BMS office contact details and the clubs and committees lists were found on the official website.\n- Instagram could only be read at profile level (names and follower counts). Posts and bios are behind a login.\n- The clubs and committees pages were last updated in September 2023, before the BMS programme began in 2025. They mainly describe the MBA campus, so they need checking against what BMS students actually have.\n- Several items in the data checklist (parcel desk, sports rosters, group membership, announcement channels, Time Tax observations, brand assets) are not public and must come from you.\n\n## 1. BMS Office information\n\n| Field | What was found | Status |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Office phone | 01704-277313 and 9950606596 | Official (contact page, updated 04/06/2026) |\n| Emails | ugadmissions@iimsirmaur.ac.in, bmsvlmchair@iimsirmaur.ac.in, bmsvlmoffice@iimsirmaur.ac.in | Official, but see note below |\n| BMS campus | Classes and accommodation for BMS are at the temporary campus in Paonta Sahib | Official (accommodation page) |\n| Main address | Dhaula Kuan, District Sirmaur, Himachal Pradesh 173031 | Official |\n| Fees and dates | Total fee of Rs 22,73,000 for 2025-29; registration 18 August 2025; classes from 21 August 2025 | Unverified (taken from a student\'s uploaded offer letter on Scribd) |\n\n**Note on the emails:** the "bmsvlm" in two addresses looks like BMS Virtual Learning Mode, the separate programme for HCLTech employees. Confirm which address the on-campus BMS office uses.\n\n**Not available online:** office hours, room or building at Paonta Sahib, appointment process, forms and required documents.\n\n## 2. Clubs (official clubs page)\n\n| Club | Focus | Notable details |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Atithya | Tourism | Inter-college activities, live projects from firms such as MakeMyTrip |\n| Capital 51 | Trading and investment | Sessions, quizzes, virtual trading competitions |\n| Consulere | Consulting | Umbrella club for marketing, operations, HR and finance |\n| Sapient | Consulting and strategy | Case contests, workshops, placement training |\n| Darpan | Literary | Book meetings, book exchange, poetry recitation, creative writing |\n| Datonics | IT and analytics | Analytics certifications, workshops, case competitions |\n| EBSB | Ek Bharat Shrestha Bharat | Himachal Pradesh and Kerala cultural pairing; events such as Mystify quiz and Onam |\n| Finserve | Finance | Flagship event Apple-o-nomics |\n| Horizon | HR | Case studies, quizzes, simulations |\n| Markaizen | Marketing | Guest lectures, conclaves, Marketing Mandli discussions |\n| ProdMan | Product management | Competitions, workshops, live projects |\n| Quizzar | Quizzing | Flagship event The King of Clubs, Cells, and Committees; inter-college Controquiz KnAwQs |\n| RangManch | Arts | Performances, Dandiya Night, YouTube presence |\n| Scope | Operations and supply chain | Industry visits, Six Sigma and project management certifications |\n| Vibgyor | Photography | Platform for members to share their work |\n\n## 3. Committees and cells (official committees page)\n\n- **Alumni Cell:** liaison with alumni; Reminiscence mentorship series; alumni portal.\n- **E&I Cell:** entrepreneurship and incubation; guest lectures, mentoring, investor networking.\n- **Infra & IT Committee:** onboarding, hostel allotment, inventory issues, support for clubs and committees.\n- **IRS (Industrial Relations and Sponsorship):** live projects, guest lectures, industry visits, sponsorships.\n- **Media Cell:** manages the institute\'s social media and merchandise; covers events.\n- **Naivedyam (Mess Committee):** menu updated monthly, festive food, Food Nights, student feedback.\n- **Placement Committee:** student-run; live projects, internships, guest lectures (Colloquium). A separate Placement Committee (BMS) page exists on the site but was not read.\n- **Sankalp (CSR Cell):** donation drives and CSR events.\n- **Sanskriti (Cultural Committee):** festivals and the annual fest Sierra.\n- **Sports Committee:** intra- and inter-college events including the Sirmaur Premier League; facilities include football, badminton, volleyball, gym, table tennis, foosball, snooker and pool.\n- **Student Academic Committee (SAC):** attendance records, academic feedback and grievances, exam support.\n- **Student Council:** six elected representatives: President, Treasurer, and Infrastructure, Sports, Mess and Cultural Secretaries.\n- **T&D Cell:** CV vetting, mock GDs and interviews.\n- **TEDx IIM Sirmaur:** organises the annual TEDx event.\n\n## 4. Instagram accounts found\n\n| Account | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| @iim\\_sirmaur | Official institute account, run by @mediacom.iimsirmaur |\n| @sierra.iimsirmaur | Annual fest, Paonta Sahib |\n| @sportscommittee\\_iimsirmaur | Official Sports Committee page |\n| @rangmanch\\_iimsirmaur | Official page of the arts club |\n| @bmsbadminton\\_ | BMS Badminton Club; the only BMS-specific account found, official status unverified |\n\nNo Instagram accounts were found for the other clubs. Quizzar and Finserve appear on LinkedIn only.\n\n## 5. Gaps and things to check\n\n**Likely outdated or MBA-focused**\n\n- The clubs and committees pages date from September 2023.\n- One third-party site says the first BMS batch set up its own student council and clubs, but this is unverified. Ask a BMS student or the Student Council which clubs are active.\n\n**Not publicly available (needed from you)**\n\n1. Parcel desk process: collection point, hours, who logs arrivals, how recipients are matched.\n2. Sports teams: captains, roster limits, registration rules, fixtures and venues.\n3. Group memberships: section groups, project teams, organizers.\n4. Announcement channels: which WhatsApp groups, email lists or notice boards, and who may post.\n5. Time Tax observations: service, date and time, waiting duration, queue count, method and sample size.\n6. Brand assets: logo, final name, permitted photos, short description, support contact.\n7. Club contacts, recruitment links and dates, and logos (only people who have agreed to be listed).\n8. BMS office hours, location, forms and appointment process.\n9. Instagram details that need a login: bios, recruitment posts, event dates (screenshots or pasted text are enough).\n\n## 6. Next steps\n\n1. Send the full CampusOS project (the earlier zip held only the chatbot files) so the data can be mapped to the right files.\n2. Collect the missing items above.\n3. Load the verified data, label each item as official or unverified, and extend the chatbot to answer questions about the BMS office, clubs and committees.\n\n## Sources\n\n- IIM Sirmaur contact details: https://iimsirmaur.ac.in/en/contact-details\n- BMS accommodation: https://iimsirmaur.ac.in/accommodation\n- Student clubs: https://iimsirmaur.ac.in/hi/node/262\n- Student committees: https://www.iimsirmaur.ac.in/hi/node/182\n- Vibrant campus: https://iimsirmaur.ac.in/en/vibrant-campus-1\n- Instagram: instagram.com/iim\\_sirmaur, sierra.iimsirmaur, sportscommittee\\_iimsirmaur, rangmanch\\_iimsirmaur, bmsbadminton\\_\n- Offer letter (unverified): https://www.scribd.com/document/907608252/Offer-Letter\n- MSM Unify (third-party): https://www.msmunify.com/in/college/iim-sirmaur\n\n',
